FORMANCE, CHALLENGES & EXPECTED BEHAVIOR\n","=============================================================================\n","\n","1. Model Performance Summary:\n","   - All 6 models demonstrated exceptional classification capability (>99.6% Accuracy).\n","   - Support Vector Machine (SVM), K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), and Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP)\n","     achieved perfect 100.00% Accuracy, Recall, and F1-Score on the test set.\n","   - Logistic Regression and Random Forest followed closely with 99.94% Accuracy and 99.87% Recall.\n","   - Decision Tree achieved 99.69% Accuracy and 99.49% Recall.\n","\n","2. Safety-Critical Metric (Recall & False Negatives):\n","   - In mushroom edibility classification, predicting a poisonous mushroom as edible (False Negative)\n","     is life-threatening. Therefore, Recall for the poisonous class was the primary optimization metric.\n","   - Models achieving 100.00% Recall (SVM, KNN, MLP) are clinically superior as they eliminate fatal misclassifications.\n","\n","3. Interpretability vs. Black-Box Trade-Off:\n","   - Decision Tree: Highly interpretable decision rules (visible splits on principal components).\n","   - Logistic Regression: Offers transparent feature coefficients and odds ratios.\n","   - SVM and MLP: Act as black-box models with superior margin separation and non-linear mapping.\n","\n","4. Computational Trade-offs & Training Efficiency:\n","   - Decision Tree and Logistic Regression trained almost instantaneously (<1 second).\n","   - KNN required zero training time but higher test query computation.\n","   - Random Forest and MLP required more computational iterations for backpropagation and tree aggregation.\n","=============================================================================\n","\"\"\"\n","print(discussion_text)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"tVvrzv6bFpcc","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791053301427,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":21,"user":{"displayName"